<% content_for :title, "Service level agreement" %>
<% content_for :description, "What HardPoint commits to for shops on the Business and Enterprise plans: 99.9% monthly uptime, service credits when we miss it, and how fast we answer when a till can't sell." %>

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold">Service level agreement</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-gray-500">What HardPoint commits to for shops on the <strong>Business</strong> and <strong>Enterprise</strong> plans, as part of the <%= link_to "terms of service", terms_path, class: "link" %>. Starter shops get the same service without the commitments below. Last changed <%= l(Date.new(2026, 11, 8), format: :long) %>.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Uptime</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">HardPoint is available at least <strong>99.9% of each calendar month</strong>: about 44 minutes of downtime a month at most. Downtime is any period of five minutes or more in which no shop can sign in or sell online, as measured by our monitoring from outside our servers. It doesn't include announced maintenance, faults in Safaricom, Airtel, KRA, Paystack or your own internet connection or devices, or time when your till kept selling offline.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Maintenance</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Updates that need downtime happen between <strong>02:00 and 04:00 East Africa Time</strong>, announced in HardPoint at least 24 hours before, and only when needed. Most updates need no downtime and aren't announced.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Your data</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Every change is copied off our servers continuously, so if a server is lost we restore to within <strong>five minutes</strong> of the failure and aim to be selling again within <strong>30 minutes</strong>. Shops' own backups (Settings › Your data) are kept on a separate service in a different place.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Support</h2>
  <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="table text-sm">
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Starter</th><th>Business</th><th>Enterprise</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="font-medium">How</td><td>WhatsApp, email, the help centre</td><td>WhatsApp, email, phone</td><td>WhatsApp, email, phone, a named contact</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="font-medium">Hours</td><td>09:00–18:00 Mon–Sat</td><td>09:00–18:00 Mon–Sat</td><td>07:00–20:00 every day</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="font-medium">A till can't sell</td><td>Next business day</td><td><strong>Within 2 hours</strong></td><td><strong>Within 1 hour</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="font-medium">Anything else</td><td>Within 2 business days</td><td>Within 1 business day</td><td>Within 1 business day</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="font-medium">Review</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>A call every quarter</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">"A till can't sell" means no till in the shop can record a sale, online or offline. A report that's wrong or a feature that's missing is "anything else". Response times are within the support hours of your plan.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">If we miss it</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">If availability in a month falls below 99.9% for a Business or Enterprise shop, we credit <strong>10% of that month's subscription for every full hour</strong> below the commitment, up to 50% of the month, against your next invoice. Ask within 30 days of the end of the month from the Billing page or by email. Credits are the whole remedy for missing the uptime commitment, and apply to the subscription, not to setup, training or hardware.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Telling you what's happening</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-gray-700">During an incident we post what we know in HardPoint's announcements and on our status page, and we email every affected shop's owners afterwards with what happened and what we've changed.</p>
</article>
